FINDINGS:

1. [MAJOR] src/lsp.rs:2539-2548 — `interpolations_in` calls `matching_close` (src/lsp.rs:3130-3143) for **every** balanced `{`, and `matching_close` itself restarts a forward scan from that open; for a literal of nested braces (`"{{{{…}}}}"`) this is O(n²), and each candidate additionally runs `is_complete_expression` (lex + parse of the inner text). This is exactly the quadratic pattern the parser avoids by advancing past a matched pair (`index = scan + 1`, src/parser.rs:2999; its comment at 2943-2946 claims the walk is linear). Worse, `references_globally` invokes `interpolations_in` for every Text token on every `find_references` query (src/lsp.rs:2648-2652) and then re-runs `analyze` over the whole file once per interpolation (src/lsp.rs:2653-2655), so a file with M interpolations costs O(M·file_size), and a large/pathological literal can hang the language server. Fix: pair braces in one linear stack pass and skip a matched span the way the parser does; skip literals whose decoded text cannot contain the queried name; and cap or memoize the per-literal analyses instead of re-analyzing the file for every pair. VERIFIED: traced `interpolations_in` → `matching_close` per open and the per-interpolation `analyze` loop; the parser counterpart's linear `index = scan + 1` advance confirms the LSP path is the quadratic one.

2. [MINOR] tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:4496-4510 — every new interpolation-reference test projects the result to `(line, column)` and never asserts `end_line`/`end_column`, so the new end-mapping branch in `InterpolationSource::original_location` (src/lsp.rs:2429-2438, the `literal.sources`/suffix path) is never checked. The goto test's `end_column` at tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:4482-4491 is the declaration in the prefix (identity mapping), and the escaped-brace test at 4564-4573 also only checks starts, so a wrong end span for an interpolated use would pass the suite. Also, `find_references` on a **builtin inside** an interpolation (`find_references_in_interpolation` with `target == None`, src/lsp.rs:2743-2752 → `references_globally` with `declaration == None`) has no test at all; only goto has a builtin-in-interpolation test (tests/tooling_grammar_test.rs:4513-4529). Add assertions on `end_column` for `"message: {greeting}"` (and a use that ends the expression / follows an escaped brace), plus a `find_references(source, 1, 8)` case for `say "{abs(-3)}"`.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 2
